✔ csv reader: quoted fields, thousands separators and a trailing row survive the bank export format (0.845083ms)
✔ statement import: the file is the only source, its content digest blocks a second import, and a file that does not add up is refused (4092.86525ms)
✔ an imported bank line is never edited: correction is cancelling the whole batch, and only before a match on it is approved (4499.576833ms)
✔ suggestion explains itself in words and stays a suggestion: nothing is matched without a human, and the preparer never approves (4386.784833ms)
✔ tenant isolation and capability: a user of another entity and a user without the capability see and touch nothing (4361.103125ms)
✔ a bank rule only suggests: it names an account and an owner and posts nothing (4049.325125ms)
✔ period reconciliation: every line is decided first, the difference is shown, and an approved reconciliation is locked (4416.940583ms)
✔ a non-zero difference is never stored or approved without a written explanation (4381.109208ms)
✔ eligibility: tenure is counted in calendar months, month ends clamp, and the day before the boundary is not yet eligible (1.472167ms)
✔ the employee view: what I have from the contract, my insurance with masked numbers, and when I become eligible (4422.690708ms)
✔ privacy: only the employee and the benefits capability see «مزاياي», dependants and benefit documents (4489.916375ms)
✔ dependant add and remove: the employee requests, HR confirms, and medical dependants are updated through benefits.mjs (4293.4575ms)
✔ HR never decides their own benefit request, and the employee can withdraw only while it is pending (4052.875292ms)
✔ draft until accepted: nothing is claimable from a draft, the proposer never accepts, and the matrix needs a written basis (4369.708208ms)
✔ ticket claim chain: employee, then HR sets the class and amount, then a different person in finance confirms; money is only proposed (4366.616209ms)
✔ the ticket option waits for tenure, and class upgrade and education follow the accepted policy only (4412.507125ms)
✔ the screens render for every role without undefined values or inline styles, and every offered button opens a usable form (4338.618708ms)
✔ notifications open the right screen and the unread list reads them (4251.242417ms)
✔ ticket claim year at the Riyadh boundary: a claim made at 00:30 Riyadh on 1 January is that year's one claim (5191.364125ms)
✔ the medical policy is a record of what the insurer holds, and the screen says the platform is not connected to any insurer (4409.813333ms)
✔ dependant data is third-party personal data: only the benefits capability reads it, and no report or export carries it (4572.116083ms)
✔ no medical information can be stored at all: the schema offers no column that would accept it (3997.896125ms)
✔ enrolment records an action taken at the insurer: never for yourself, never twice, and only in a tier of the policy (4198.228334ms)
✔ the screen reminds what must be done at the insurer: nobody is added or removed by the platform itself (4293.894958ms)
✔ an isolated tenant account reads and writes nothing of the other tenant benefits (4215.39575ms)
✔ the benefits screen renders for every role and every offered button opens a usable form (4424.700416ms)
✔ a recurring schedule prepares a draft for the period and never an issued invoice, and rerunning it changes nothing (4691.248417ms)
✔ an advance is a liability whose receipt a second person confirms, and drawn amounts never exceed the paid balance (4128.7975ms)
✔ carry-forward and overage deduction are independent contract options that move entitlement only, never the invoice amount (4135.180083ms)
✔ usage thresholds are configuration set by the contract owner, and each threshold alerts once per period (4419.201916ms)
✔ recurring billing is closed to accounts without the capability and never reaches another tenant (4389.2265ms)
