✔ registry: validateSpec refuses what would break a page — mask paradoxes, unknown capabilities, banned or duplicate status phrases, governed fields, and edits that lose recorded data (6250.697084ms)
✔ registry: a draft built on a version that is no longer live is refused at publish, and re-saving rebases it (4739.532167ms)
✔ registry: renaming the client entity «العميل» to «الجهة» reaches every label that inherits from it at once, and one click takes it back (4273.860625ms)
✔ registry: the snapshot a browser receives is masked per user — not even the definition, label or options of a field the reader may not see — and answers «unchanged» to a matching digest (4182.33825ms)
✔ registry: an unsubmitted draft is not readable by other holders of the capability — the promise the drawer makes is kept by the server (4159.844125ms)
✔ registry: the published-definition cache holds one entry per entity, not one per version, and a board asks for the chain head once (4631.5775ms)
✔ transfer: export then import into a fresh database yields an identical published state, and the diff report shown before applying is truthful (8787.044625ms)
✔ transfer: what was shown is what is applied — a target that changed after the check refuses the apply until it is checked again, and everything lands atomically (8969.109208ms)
✔ transfer: a bundle that loosens a control is not applied by the person who checked it, and the target learns how many of its records use an option the bundle retires (8573.722125ms)
✔ transfer: a bundle edited by hand, from another format, or naming what this environment does not know is refused or blocked before anything is compared (12293.861167ms)
✔ transfer: the routes and the command-line twin run the same functions — export, check, apply between two database files, never the preview database itself (12230.289916ms)
✔ transfer: a bundle that deletes a published option is blocked, not reported as an addition — the records that chose it keep their label (8577.327ms)
✔ transfer: two environments whose published documents differ only in order are reported as different, not «identical» (8565.150291ms)
✔ delivery cycle: no step of the client chain opens before the step before it was approved by someone else (4200.895208ms)
✔ delivery cycle: an entitlement is born from an accepted deliverable only — a submitted one is not enough (4637.65125ms)
✔ delivery cycle: the customer invoice hangs on an approved entitlement, and the preparer never issues it (4532.605125ms)
✔ delivery cycle: collection is recorded and matched by two people and never exceeds the entitlement (4193.286042ms)
✔ delivery cycle: a client review stage closes only on an external approval documented against that very version (4455.550208ms)
✔ delivery cycle: no supplier award without a comparison, a qualified vendor and an approved project budget (5618.233ms)
✔ delivery cycle: the supplier is not received, invoiced or paid before the purchase order, and the payment needs three separate people (7855.679125ms)
✔ delivery cycle: execution is blocked until the advance payment is confirmed (5717.152583ms)
✔ delivery cycle: a supplier may not start before a purchase order AND a commencement authorisation (4847.3985ms)
✔ delivery cycle: the customer purchase order is recorded against the commercial case before execution (4346.804666ms)
✔ delivery cycle: a project can be closed technically and then financially (4230.310292ms)
✔ delivery cycle: paying the supplier marks the purchase as paid, read from payment_orders not from a constant (4919.237584ms)
✔ delivery cycle: work packages can be planned for more than one department (4418.2485ms)
✔ delivery cycle: a finance delegation is granted, expires and is revoked through the platform, never by a direct insert (4622.637542ms)
✔ delivery cycle: the completion certificate is a numbered, versioned record, and the client acceptance is employee-entered evidence with its stated limit, never a signature (4544.878917ms)
✔ التفويض المالي له سقف مدة، ورقمه هو ما تستعمله المنصة فعلًا لا رقم مستعار (5035.623458ms)
