✔ the written-defence window is labelled a company-set period, and Art. 117 is cited only for what it says (4337.51375ms)
✔ the employee is told the defence window is the company’s, not the regulation’s (4139.964083ms)
✔ the shared-penalty cell follows the signed pages: a preparer clears items 1–5 and 11, and removing a cell is as available as adding one (4303.505042ms)
✔ a shared-penalty correction is validated: only the values the signed tables print, and never mixed with an occurrence cell (4409.627291ms)
✔ schedule: the regulation extract is seeded as a platform draft with every row cited, two flagged cells, and nothing applies until the HR manager accepts a company version (4380.11225ms)
✔ Art. 114: repeats are counted within 180 days of the previous same violation, and a gap of 181 days starts again at one (4161.329625ms)
✔ Art. 114: only penalties that stand are counted — withdrawn, unproven and grievance-cancelled cases do not raise the next occurrence (4556.107958ms)
✔ Art. 115: one act that breaks several items gets only the harshest penalty, once (4346.625292ms)
✔ Art. 113: the authority may choose a lighter penalty with a written reason, never a harsher one (4935.074459ms)
✔ Arts. 117 and 126(1): above a one-day fine a written charge, hearing minutes and a defence (or its window) come before any finding; oral questioning is for minor penalties only (5804.499667ms)
✔ Arts. 119 and 120: no investigation after 30 days from discovery and no penalty after 30 days from proof; both show countdowns and close as time-barred (4579.44225ms)
✔ separation of duties: nobody records against themselves, the recorder and the subject never decide, and the decider does not issue the notice (4229.96725ms)
✔ Art. 121: the penalty notice is a bilingual HR-initiated letter; delivery is recorded by hand, registered mail or the contract email, and a refusal to sign needs a second delivery (4260.747ms)
✔ Art. 126: the grievance window is 30 days excluding official holidays, the answer is due in 15, the outcome is never harsher, and filing pauses the payroll deduction (4560.828458ms)
✔ payroll: a decided fine reaches payroll only as a proposed deduction, capped at five days’ wage a month, and never approved by the platform (4427.296375ms)
✔ no automatic penalty: attendance days are evidence only, a late day never opens a case by itself, and absence items need a confirmed unpaid absence (4327.726208ms)
✔ privacy: the employee alone sees their case in full; colleagues learn nothing, the manager sees a summary, and evidence follows the case (4172.528541ms)
✔ penalty helpers: labels, occurrence tiers past the last cell, and the empty fourth cell (0.496084ms)
✔ integration: an open discipline case counts as an open investigation for the resignation clock, and a withdrawn one does not (4159.376958ms)
✔ مرجع القضية يُشتق من أعلى رقم مستعمل، فلا تعيده فجوة في التسلسل إلى رقم سبق أن استُعمل (4413.024042ms)
✔ the only built-in gateway is disconnected: it refuses all three calls, sends nothing, and says so (1.427666ms)
✔ issuing a document archives it and queues it in the same statement, and the archive can never be edited or deleted (4224.728083ms)
✔ the counter never resets, never skips and never goes back, and the hash chain link is enforced by the database itself (4545.03225ms)
✔ whoever classifies the channel never performs the attempt, the channel is fixed once set, and a stale version is refused (4471.150917ms)
✔ today an attempt sends nothing: the refusal is logged with its reason and the next attempt backs off exponentially (5264.242333ms)
✔ an injected gateway drives every queue state, a decision is final, and a rejected document keeps its number and its place in the counter (5749.5285ms)
✔ a buyer with missing tax data blocks the attempt until a documented override is recorded, and the override is permanent (4273.018666ms)
✔ a complete buyer needs no override, and a credit note is archived with the reference of its original invoice (4151.94ms)
✔ the screen needs the einvoice capability, and another tenant sees and touches nothing (4328.077666ms)
✔ migration 151: the database checks clean, and every index and trigger on the rebuilt table is back (3750.089958ms)
✔ migration 151: the constraint accepts only the dated approved rates, and the document codes cannot drift from the document (4482.455583ms)
✔ migration 151: a document line without a unit code is refused by the database itself (4975.911292ms)
✔ every control carries one of four verdicts and evidence from the code, and the report never claims compliance (4618.913041ms)
✔ the verdicts match what the platform really does: deletion and counter reset fail, and what was not checked is not guessed (4341.22025ms)
✔ the report is computed from the live schema: a removed guard or a tampered document turns its control to not met (4845.025334ms)
✔ an injected gateway is reported as such, and the report needs the einvoice capability inside its own tenant (5928.404583ms)
✔ employee assistant: answers leave balance for the asker only, explains how a service is requested and who approves it, quotes policy, and refuses the rest (5809.254083ms)
✔ employee assistant with a model: only the retrieved facts are sent, inside the data fence, and another person’s balance never leaves the database (4619.649875ms)
✔ career profile and development plan: the profile is the employee’s own, a qualification is verified by someone else, and the plan draft uses only that profile (4321.003958ms)
✔ بوابة الموظف تحمل كل خدمة يحق للحساب طلبها، بلا نسخة يدوية ناقصة (5697.653625ms)
