✔ ER-01: a case whose accepted terms require neither condition behaves exactly as before, and the terms say whether a customer PO is required (4384.112583ms)
✔ ER-02: every paid-execution entry point is checked on the server at the moment of action (4284.76475ms)
✔ ER-03: an exemption is requested by one person and authorised by another, with written reasons, and both sides are auditable (4250.17875ms)
✔ ER-04: the exemption is rechecked at the moment of action — withdrawn, or held by someone who lost the authority, it no longer opens the gate (8654.342583ms)
✔ ER-05: partial, duplicate and reversed receipts — only money that arrived once and stayed opens the gate (4591.359ms)
✔ ER-06: the customer PO is versioned and append-only — superseded, expired or unconfirmed versions never satisfy the gate (4354.012917ms)
✔ ER-07: the order is checked against its own case — wrong client, opportunity, agreement, project or tenant is refused (4545.363792ms)
✔ ER-08: another tenant's receipt never satisfies the gate, and a bank reference is unique within a tenant only (4166.6535ms)
✔ ER-09: concurrency — the gate and the action share one write lock, so a reversal racing a delivery submission lands before it or after it, never between (4431.371208ms)
✔ ER-10: the actions are reachable over HTTP with the platform session, CSRF and idempotency, and the commercial screen names the blockers (6159.011542ms)
✔ ER-11: the billing screen asks for the bank reference, offers the reversal once, and links an advance to its project (4207.290916ms)
✔ executive routes parse their range and keep named details behind source access (5242.135041ms)
✔ cockpit renders truth state and accessible drilldown controls (23.127792ms)
✔ cockpit limits the first view and escapes source text (1.5505ms)
✔ metric form explains withheld details without inventing rows (0.525375ms)
✔ a missing cash source is unavailable, never zero (4207.455791ms)
✔ the cockpit has six aggregate dimensions and keeps the legacy board contract (4153.547584ms)
✔ named drilldown stays behind the source capability while the aggregate remains visible (4376.177209ms)
✔ metric definitions are versioned and cannot be rewritten after use (4110.792666ms)
✔ the metric contract carries its source and refuses incomplete or invented values (4297.305625ms)
✔ executive scope: the holder of executive.view reads every project in the entity, while the membership board he calls is untouched (4441.871625ms)
✔ executive scope: a project member without executive.view is refused by both new functions, and the capability is the only door (4261.621292ms)
✔ executive scope: the portfolio forecast carries the funnel numbers and its warning, and not one opportunity, client or loss comment (4195.883375ms)
✔ executive scope: the executive board carries the portfolio counts for the capability holder and for nobody else (4534.183583ms)
✔ المؤشر التنفيذي يقيس المكتمل مقابل زمن الخدمة ويستبعد غير القابل للقياس (4396.218125ms)
✔ E51: a receipt is claimed once, approved by the line manager then finance, and the claimant decides nothing (4161.439125ms)
✔ E52: custody is issued by finance, settled by approved claims, and closes only when the remainder is returned exactly (4391.836292ms)
✔ E61: an asset is approved by a second person and depreciates straight-line once per month with no gaps, the last month absorbing rounding (4469.088459ms)
✔ ledger: expense, custody, depreciation and the year-end close all post from their documents and keep the balance sheet balanced (4156.537292ms)
✔ expiry watch: the platform never assumes a reminder window — an expiry is only called “due soon” after its owner records the window with its source (4184.253375ms)
✔ expiry watch: only the owner of the procedure records a window, the second write carries the version it read, and an unordered pair is refused (4218.977166ms)
✔ expiry watch: an account is shown only the expiries it may open in detail, its own always, and never another tenant’s (4343.06525ms)
✔ expiry sources: hands the shared decision box rows it can absorb unchanged, and keeps valid documents out of it (4271.248542ms)
✔ expiry watch: a fixed-term contract end is watched like any other expiry, and only its holder and the contracts owner see it (4164.998041ms)
✔ expiry watch: the watched kinds are exactly the expiry dates the existing tables really carry (4434.168375ms)
✔ expiry screen: renders for every seeded role, offers the window form only to the owner of that kind, and never asks for a duration it invented (4079.345625ms)
✔ one-to-one: the content belongs to the two parties, each private note to its writer alone, and HR sees that it happened and when — never what was said (4310.698209ms)
✔ one-to-one follow-up items belong to their owner: only the owner closes one, and open items surface on the owner’s own list (4350.97325ms)
✔ a feedback note is owned by its author and its recipient: visibility alone decides who else reads it, and HR is no exception (4427.79625ms)
✔ feedback is requested with a specific question, and what the evaluator may see reaches the review cycle as evidence — never copied into it and never scored (4401.999416ms)
✔ 360: the panel is approved by a third party — not the subject, not the nominator, not the rater (4216.479833ms)
✔ 360: upward feedback is never revealed below the threshold the HR manager set, the threshold lives in the query, and no source is scored or ranked (4391.556042ms)
✔ files: type comes from the content signature, access follows the record, restricted bank proofs need the finance grant, and nothing is overwritten (4552.191875ms)
✔ MFA policy: once required, a sensitive capability works only for accounts with two-step verification, and only the first admin sets the policy (4498.218ms)
✔ criterion 15: a backup is proven by restoring it elsewhere and passing integrity, foreign-key, audit-chain and invoice-chain checks (4715.177833ms)
