✔ HTTP: files are listed per record, uploaded once per key, downloaded as sandboxed attachments, and the policy route is first-admin only (5851.494625ms)
✔ ledger screen: a payable paid inside a grouped order reads paid, a returned transfer is not payment, and a supplier credit lowers what is owed (4589.0075ms)
✔ exceptions: each kind is computed from its source with its owner, and what already waits as a decision elsewhere is listed but not counted in the inbox twice (4730.204792ms)
✔ acknowledgement: an append-only record by the owner, at the amount of the moment; it leaves the inbox, comes back when the amount changes, and is refused to anyone else (4910.828ms)
✔ overdue re-close: a reopened month past its re-close date is an exception for whoever manages the close (4434.982458ms)
✔ screen and routes: the queue renders each exception with its owner and an acknowledge form, and the route acknowledges once per idempotency key through the real handler (5318.597416ms)
✔ audit package: the queue offers the period package as a download to whoever also holds the audit capability, and to no one else (4466.453375ms)
✔ finance periods: a monthly close never rides on a year-long accounting period, and the rest of the year stays postable (4172.292583ms)
✔ finance periods: the database itself refuses a close period bound to an accounting period that is not exactly its month (4310.5365ms)
✔ finance periods: a month approved with no accounting period is not called locked, because its entries are not (4155.751542ms)
✔ suppliers: the ledger statement, R32, the executive pulse, the cash forecast and the project settlement axis all read payable_balances — a batch, a partial payment, a return and a supplier credit note included (4390.529541ms)
✔ customers: the ledger statement, R31 aging, the executive pulse and the cash forecast read ar_claim_collection — a reversed receipt is not collected, a credit note lowers the claim, an allocation settles it (4619.844ms)
✔ project closure: the journals line counts the project's advance receipt, draw and reversal, a batch payment through its lines, and a returned supplier payment (4440.2435ms)
✔ trace: a batch payment settles every invoice it pays, by the part it paid, and the payment names each invoice it settles (4575.091125ms)
✔ AP aging: each open payable is aged from its due date — the verified tax invoice date plus the owner's payment term — at its outstanding balance, and without an adopted term it says so and ages from the invoice date (4413.896333ms)
✔ R35 is the close checks themselves: unposted journals (never a rejected one), documents without a posted journal, an active bank account without an approved reconciliation, and each control difference, every row with an owner and a named item (4658.946208ms)
✔ margin: supplier cost enters the project margin net of verified input VAT and of approved supplier credit notes, against net revenue — and verifying the VAT later moves the figures an acceptance was taken on (4472.094959ms)
✔ cash forecast: the opening balance comes from the ledger balance of reconciled bank accounts plus final cash documents not yet posted; a typed figure is refused while a reconciliation exists, and stays labelled manual when none does (4108.581625ms)
✔ FIN-01/06/09: a balanced journal reaches an immutable local posting and a sourced trial balance (4168.094375ms)
✔ FIN-01/06: unbalanced, floating, negative, empty or two-sided amounts cannot create a journal (4585.01325ms)
✔ FIN-06: returned revisions require a fresh independent approval and cannot skip posting (4323.437458ms)
✔ FIN-06/09: a closed period and deactivated reference block a pending posting (4334.221542ms)
✔ FIN-06: an exact reversal is prepared and approved separately, then offsets the ledger once (4338.542666ms)
✔ IT-02/PLT-05: financial reads and writes require current explicit unexpired grants (4295.134459ms)
✔ FIN-06: posting checks whether the original approver still holds authority (4331.288542ms)
✔ FIN-05/06: a matched procurement reference creates one exact payable journal (4372.075375ms)
✔ FIN-06 PLT-06/09: idempotent creation and rollback preserve one journal and its audit (4374.676833ms)
✔ the cited source file opens: every form points at a document that exists, and the two recovered documents came back as they were (2.491625ms)
✔ the HR forms never cite the project-cycle register, because that register does not mention their folder at all (0.626958ms)
✔ the eight forms of the templates folder are built, and the register and the catalogue say the same thing about each (0.919708ms)
✔ every field of the eight carries its own basis: the name of its Drive file, or a written reason why it has none (0.171334ms)
✔ what was never read is declared, not dressed up: the unread templates stay pending, and their unreadable files are listed (0.286958ms)
✔ the structure that was read is reproduced in the original order, so the record renders as the company form (0.182542ms)
✔ electronic all the way: no signature field and no identity-number field, and every approval seat is one the platform actually has (0.455625ms)
✔ the eight seed as drafts nobody can fill, and an accepted one runs the ordinary electronic chain end to end (4384.932209ms)
✔ the gate the template imposes is checked at the electronic approval, and a refused receiving manager blocks it (4208.108834ms)
✔ المنح المحصور بإدارة يُخزَّن بإدارته: الحصر مكتوب في الصف لا مُدَّعى على الشاشة (4226.048584ms)
✔ المعتمد المحصور بإدارة أخرى لا يقرأ النسخة المملوءة (4265.50925ms)
✔ المعتمد المحصور بإدارة أخرى لا يعتمد ولا يعيد ولا يرفض (4187.50625ms)
✔ والحصر لا يُغلق على من يصله: معتمد إدارة المعبّئ يقرأ ويعتمد كما كان (4207.69ms)
