✔ compensatory review: an exit payout never goes to a month with no payroll line — a locked exit month names who reopens it, and the hours stay due (4293.236416ms)
✔ compensatory review: when the exit month is already approved no run can carry the pay — it is an open item on the settlement, carried by a written decision and kept with it (4286.180708ms)
✔ compensatory review: leave approved for a date after the service ended is not «used» — it blocks the settlement until it is cancelled, then its hours are paid (4446.308125ms)
✔ compensatory review: a hand-written overtime movement is refused while leave-compensated hours are unsettled — next month and before approval too — and the approver sees one that came first (4203.281375ms)
✔ compensatory review: hours past their deadline are not leave any more, even for a back-dated request — the payout queue does not shrink under the preparer (4274.178458ms)
✔ compensatory review: a working-time policy accepted between reservation and approval does not debit a day at the old length — the request goes back to be reserved again (4300.571ms)
✔ compensatory review: split payouts of one credit never return more overtime than was worked, at a ratio that does not divide evenly (4226.851834ms)
✔ compensatory review: the company cap on overtime pay (Art. 77(5)) never blocks the pay of unused compensatory hours — the approver is told, and decides (4410.215833ms)
✔ compensatory review: the employee never sees a fake zero — «غير متاح» with its reason when no policy is accepted, and approved hours not yet credited are shown to their owner (8594.715208ms)
✔ compensatory review: the payroll pre-run check counts what is really due — a credit still inside its deadline is a notice, not «انقضت مهلته» (4289.165417ms)
✔ compensatory review: INSERT OR REPLACE cannot rewrite a recorded consent or a credit (4475.65025ms)
✔ compensatory UI: the overtime form offers the choice, shows the exact sentence the server stores, and sends consent only when ticked (8796.570959ms)
✔ compensatory UI: «الإجازات» shows the balance in hours and days with each credit's deadline and the 14-day warning; attendance shows the queues to their holders only (4613.966042ms)
✔ leave law 2025: every type cites the labor law beside the company regulation, and nothing the regulation grants is lowered (2.556917ms)
✔ leave law 2025: Hajj leave — two years of service, once, ten to fifteen calendar days including Eid, with an electronic declaration (4119.653583ms)
✔ leave law 2025: the yearly number of Hajj leaves is the company's to set — an open question until written, enforced once it is (4213.155708ms)
✔ leave law 2025: exam leave without the company's approval comes from annual leave if there is any, otherwise it is unpaid as of right (Art. 115/2) (12673.51225ms)
✔ leave law 2025: a pregnant widow extends iddah without pay, and birth leave past the seventh day warns the approvers without refusing (8543.801333ms)
✔ leave law 2025: Eid days that fall on the weekly rest are compensated after the holiday (Executive Regulation Art. 24) (2.688042ms)
✔ leave law 2025: the policy assistant reads the new types with their law articles, and the HR screen shows the parameters, the sources and what is not built (4188.143375ms)
✔ leave law 2025: the draft form lets HR set the compensatory ratio and deadline, in hours per hour and days, within the legal bounds (4166.38475ms)
✔ leave law 2025: exam days are never left without a door — in probation or at the split limit they still come from annual leave (Art. 115/2) (17110.397958ms)
✔ the regulation draft cites its articles and changes nothing until the HR manager accepts it (4031.363042ms)
✔ calendar-day and working-day types count the same range differently (4163.902458ms)
✔ sick leave tiers cross request and month boundaries: 30 full, 60 at 75%, then unpaid, proposed to payroll and never auto-approved (4166.468292ms)
✔ emergency leave takes half days: the third day may be 2.5 + 0.5, and nothing beyond (4478.648959ms)
✔ annual leave is refused during probation and allowed once it ends (4206.8725ms)
✔ unpaid leave needs a year of service and no balance left; above 5 working days it goes to the authority holder (4230.481083ms)
✔ more than 20 unpaid days stop the annual accrual for the period (Art. 86.2b, 91.6) (4186.766084ms)
✔ leave reads the approved public holidays: one source for attendance and leave (8333.99775ms)
✔ annual leave reserves and debits against the accrual engine once an accrual rule is accepted (4503.266625ms)
✔ event types, exam notice and iddah limits follow their articles (4334.54ms)
✔ the leave form, the catalog service and search all lead to the same request (4273.167917ms)
