✔ HR-04 F05/F10: employee identity and Riyadh date boundaries do not depend on names or UTC dates (4098.982834ms)
✔ HR-05 PLT-01/05: reads and actions exclude unrelated employees, tenants and technical admins (4457.508667ms)
✔ HR-05 PLT-05: every call rechecks active role and scope after account changes (4210.882667ms)
✔ HR-05 PLT-04: clients cannot choose identity, approvers, state or request days (4201.497209ms)
✔ HR-04/05 PLT-04: returned requests release their hold and resubmit an immutable new revision (4132.195542ms)
✔ HR-05 PLT-04: HR cannot finalize approval after the employee manager changes (4294.369459ms)
✔ HR-04 PLT-09: creation retries reuse one request and recheck access before returning it (4078.20975ms)
✔ HR-04 PLT-06: ledger, decisions and submitted snapshots cannot be changed or deleted (4181.71225ms)
✔ HR-04 PLT-06: an audit write failure rolls back the reservation and request together (3953.799416ms)
✔ HR-04: future effective dates, leap days and a different workweek follow the stored calendar (4132.320416ms)
✔ HR-04/05: pending cancellation releases a hold without posting a debit or refund (4236.112834ms)
✔ HR-05 F04: the local calendar includes approved authorized days and removes cancelled leave (3995.902833ms)
✔ HR-05 SEC-01: leave forms retain the selected request version and escape stored text (4435.987667ms)
✔ registry: every existing source kind is held unchanged, the new kinds join it, and another file can register its own kind (4363.915791ms)
✔ supplier invoice: net per cost centre, input VAT from the verified record, the gross liability — one balanced journal in minor units (4401.039666ms)
✔ supplier invoice: not ready until the VAT position is known, and a supplier outside the VAT register posts gross to cost (4348.858416ms)
✔ supplier invoice: one payable, one journal — the old manual path is closed, its journals stay readable, and a trigger refuses a second path (4346.465334ms)
✔ customer advances: receipt, each draw application and reversal become journals, and the control reads net of reversals (4345.24525ms)
✔ migration 167 upgrade: draws applied before it become one opening event each, and later applications are captured by the trigger (4531.267125ms)
✔ pending sources: an unposted supplier liability is listed and blocks the monthly close pack like any other unposted document (4367.946084ms)
✔ control reconciliation: AR, AP, input VAT, output VAT and customer advances tie to their control accounts after a synthetic month, and the trial balance balances (4576.652125ms)
✔ control reconciliation: every difference is itemised to a document or a journal, and the items add up to the difference (4655.787125ms)
✔ control reconciliation: read-only, finance-scoped and tenant-isolated (4482.939625ms)
✔ trace: a supplier invoice walks to its approvers, its posted journal, its payment, the bank line, and its reversal — with explicit no-link markers (4835.10075ms)
✔ trace: an invoice reaches its receipt, the advance drawn on it and its credit note; a manual journal says it has no source document (4493.765584ms)
✔ trace: finance-scoped, tenant-isolated, and it refuses what it cannot find instead of guessing (4452.7365ms)
✔ listFinance: no constant payment status; each payable carries its payment state from its payment order (4578.524083ms)
✔ idempotency: two processes preparing the same supplier invoice at the same instant leave one journal, one payable link and one source link (7288.552625ms)
✔ separation of duties: the preparer neither approves nor posts a sourced journal, a reversal needs another preparer, and a read-only holder prepares nothing (4485.659375ms)
✔ routes: GET /api/ledger/reconciliation and /api/ledger/trace answer a finance reader and refuse everyone else, writing nothing (5635.690417ms)
✔ screens: the statements screen shows the control reconciliation and a trace action; the finance screen shows each payable’s real payment state (4814.59925ms)
✔ the ledger does not reopen from the ledger screen or by a direct update: finance names the controlled path, and the database refuses the rest (4278.251ms)
✔ a checklist reopen request carries a ledger reopening; a third person with ledger authority approves it once the owner has set the re-close deadline, and the month takes a dated adjustment (4314.847042ms)
✔ re-close relocks the ledger through the same checks and records who re-closed; the reopening is used once and its history never changes (4074.277042ms)
✔ a rejected reopening leaves the ledger locked and the close approved; another tenant never sees the request (4167.176916ms)
✔ an issued invoice becomes one balanced draft journal whose lines cannot be edited or posted twice (4110.244834ms)
✔ statements come from posted journals only: invoice, credit note and receipt flow into income statement, balance sheet and the customer statement (4484.435625ms)
✔ a payroll run posts as totals only, and nothing posts without approved mappings recorded and approved by different people (4275.478459ms)
✔ F09: an unknown route is denied for every role (0.633667ms)
✔ F09: known rules and explicit empty overrides keep their meaning (0.093334ms)
✔ letter templates: the platform writes no letter text, only the approved placeholders pass, and whoever writes a template never approves it (4214.918417ms)
✔ letter types are rows, not a list in code: the procedure owner adds and retires them, and a type without an approved template cannot be requested (4441.136958ms)
✔ employment letter: the employee requests it, one person prepares and another issues, and the reference is a gapless yearly serial carrying a QR verification path (4284.810917ms)
✔ salary letter: the amount is derived from the live contract at issue time, is stored in no column, and its text reaches only its owner and whoever may issue it (4192.718292ms)
✔ letters stay inside their tenant, and SQL refuses a request whose preparer is also its issuer or its subject (4410.138542ms)
✔ lifecycle: the step template starts empty, no bundle opens without owner-defined steps, and each department owner defines only their own department’s steps (4120.472875ms)
✔ lifecycle: a dependency chain that loops back on itself is rejected on save, in code and in SQL (4389.506667ms)
✔ lifecycle: one request fans out into parallel steps; a dependent step stays visible with its reason; progress counts only steps closed with evidence; the person never closes their own journey (4308.475084ms)
✔ lifecycle: a step past its target escalates to the bundle owner as a recorded decision (4246.490333ms)
✔ clearance: the list is derived from what the platform actually knows about the person, nobody clears themselves — in code and by CHECK — and nothing is revoked or disabled automatically (4269.010666ms)
✔ clearance: the final settlement stays blocked until the financial items are closed, and a stale list cannot be used to slip past it (4119.414958ms)
✔ lifecycle: another tenant sees nothing and reaches nothing, and the screens render every value escaped under a strict CSP (4007.000875ms)
✔ LIFECYCLE: every service either closes normally or reaches its declared output-acceptance gate, and its other endings hold (13916.693875ms)
✔ links: every #view/intent literal in app/static resolves to a registered screen and a registered intent (302.076041ms)
✔ links: the catalogue card «طلب إجازة» and the search shortcuts are among what is checked, and they resolve (0.431334ms)
✔ links: the scanner treats every quoted #word as a link unless it is provably something else, so a typo cannot pass as a selector (17.32525ms)
✔ links: the screen registries cannot drift from app.mjs (0.621333ms)
