✔ KDF: the parameters are written inside the row, and a row written the old way is still read with its own parameters (2068.928625ms)
✔ KDF: both shapes verify, and only the weaker one is marked for upgrade (1852.81325ms)
✔ KDF: the floor is the recommended minimum, and one derivation costs what that floor costs on this machine (358.73425ms)
✔ KDF: a successful sign-in on an old row rewrites it with the new parameters, and nobody is signed out to do it (5602.825958ms)
✔ KDF: a changed password is written in the new shape and the old password stops working (6358.391542ms)
✔ PRC-02: an unregistered or unqualified vendor never enters the payment cycle, and no bank account means no order (12807.186875ms)
✔ FIN-07/PRC-09: approved is not paid — three people prepare, approve and record the bank execution, and the bank-detail collector cannot record it (4290.253084ms)
✔ PRC-09: if the vendor bank account changes after the order was prepared, approval stops instead of silently paying the new account (4251.443792ms)
✔ input VAT enters the summary only after a second person verifies the supplier tax invoice, and cannot exceed 15% of net (4418.417083ms)
✔ FIN-09: تمنع ضريبة الفاتورة المكررة عبر مرجع شراء آخر بعد توحيد شكل رقمها (4264.637875ms)
✔ PRC-09: يظهر توقف المورد بعد الاعتماد ويُحفظ التحذير عند توثيق تنفيذ وقع فعلا (4225.913917ms)
✔ FIN-09: السجلات القديمة المكررة لا تعتمد، ويمكن رفض المكرر ثم اعتماد الأصل (4220.968375ms)
✔ PRC-09: تغير الحساب البنكي بعد اعتماد الدفع يظهر للمالية دون كشف الآيبان (4342.752167ms)
✔ the database refuses a payment execution recorded by whoever prepared or approved the order (4128.606875ms)
✔ bank change: verifying a replacement supersedes the old account, records the change, tells finance in the platform and leaves a simulated message for the previously trusted contact (4438.182167ms)
✔ bank change: while the owner has not adopted the cooling-off days or the first-payment cap, the changed account stays blocked with a refusal naming both decisions and their owner (4626.12075ms)
✔ bank change: cooling-off counts from the verification day; afterwards the first payment is capped, released by a third person, and only then recorded as executed (4308.261459ms)
✔ bank change window: the collector and the verifier cannot prepare, approve, release or record the first payment to that vendor — refused in code and in SQL — and a returned first payment reopens the window (4534.514917ms)
✔ shared IBAN: verification is refused while the IBAN sits on another active vendor, until a separate reasoned decision by someone other than the collector allows it — and the decider does not verify (4527.203458ms)
✔ partial and batch: an order pays part of a payable or several payables of one vendor in one transfer; payableBalance tracks each step; over-allocation is refused in code and in SQL (4442.151625ms)
✔ returns: a bounced transfer is recorded once as its own record by a third person, the executed order is never edited, the balance reopens and can be paid again exactly once (4379.85475ms)
✔ adjustments: supplier credit and debit notes are append-only, reasoned and approved by a second person; they move the balance, and a credit can never go below what is paid or on its way (4397.381959ms)
✔ execution wording: every order says execution was recorded manually and simulated; the payload and the screen never claim the platform paid (4346.814459ms)
✔ vendor centre: open payables count only what is still owed — a paid payable is not open, a return reopens it (4232.757ms)
✔ tenant isolation: another tenant sees no balance, order, return or adjustment and cannot act on any of them (4598.553042ms)
✔ HTTP without a port: partial and batch orders, release, execution, return and adjustments go through the real handler; a replayed create returns the same record and a replayed step is refused (6284.529042ms)
✔ race: processes writing the same database file at the same instant never release money twice — one order for a full balance, one execution, one return, one re-payment, one first-payment release (20114.298875ms)
✔ upgrade: a database that already holds orders before 166 gets one line per order and the same balances, loses the one-order index, and its legacy vendor with two verified accounts is settled at the next verification (3487.769708ms)
✔ one bank account behind two employees is the loudest finding on the board, and no finding ever stops the run (4069.120709ms)
✔ every rule is deterministic and either has a threshold its owner entered or says plainly that it is not running (4228.032375ms)
✔ pre-payroll checks: a draft run shows what could still change it — undecided movements and missing verified salary accounts — and an approved run shows none (4153.022292ms)
✔ PAY-03: only approved adjustments enter the run, each exactly once, and a proposer or the employee cannot approve (4199.654ms)
✔ an approved advance is recovered in equal instalments through payroll and shows what is still outstanding (4096.649834ms)
✔ PAY-07: the transfer file needs a verified salary account for everyone, is released only after approval, and its execution is recorded by someone else (4270.019875ms)
✔ PAY-09: the settlement applies the accepted policy by termination class — resignation tiers differ from employer termination — and deducts outstanding advances (4163.460334ms)
✔ the case follows the join date the employee record holds, not the start of the contract he happens to be on now; and two recorded dates on opposite sides of the new law are named, never picked between (4164.933167ms)
✔ a non-Saudi is not assumed to be outside the Gulf because nobody asked: the run refuses until the question is answered where nationality is recorded, and either answer is a record (4168.266417ms)
✔ a non-Saudi is not assumed to be outside the Gulf because nobody asked: the run refuses until the question is answered where nationality is recorded, and either answer is a record [قبل الحد 2026-09-30T20:05:00.000Z] (4197.422541ms)
✔ a non-Saudi is not assumed to be outside the Gulf because nobody asked: the run refuses until the question is answered where nationality is recorded, and either answer is a record [داخل الفجوة 2026-09-30T23:05:00.000Z] (4283.542625ms)
✔ a non-Saudi is not assumed to be outside the Gulf because nobody asked: the run refuses until the question is answered where nationality is recorded, and either answer is a record [بعد الفجوة 2026-10-01T09:05:00.000Z] (4105.681375ms)
✔ the approval gate reads the rule in force, not the basis frozen on the line: a draft calculated before the rule was accepted, or before an exclusion was recorded, cannot be submitted or approved (4130.494625ms)
✔ an employee whose contract changed mid-month is charged on each part by its own wage and days, not on the newest contract for the whole month (4231.59725ms)
✔ a share clamped to what is left of the wage says so on the line, on the run and on the payslip: the percentage never prints next to an amount it does not produce (4208.73025ms)
✔ accepting the insurance rule after a month was approved does not invent a retroactive wage difference with no stated reason (4255.843083ms)
✔ the early-pay date is judged by the working week the tenant accepted, and a date confirmed by mistake is withdrawn with a written reason instead of standing for ever (4350.145416ms)
✔ the basis of an exclusion refuses an identity number however it is written: Arabic-Indic and Persian digits and digits split by dots are numbers too (4263.902125ms)
✔ when the accepted rounding rule moves the deduction, the basis carries the amount that was actually withheld — and the HR manager may keep the employee share at the halala the brief recommends (4127.667125ms)
✔ the occupational-hazards branch is in force under both laws, so a month before the date that was copied into its row still charges the company its two per cent (5430.259458ms)
✔ an age at first coverage is never applied as a figure the platform invented: nothing changes until the HR manager records a verified threshold, and then the run refuses instead of deducting (5541.839292ms)
✔ a run whose month the insurance rule never governed says the company share is unavailable, and never prints a zero it did not compute (5092.656042ms)
✔ every case in the law is deducted by its own rate: a Saudi under the previous law, a Saudi new entrant on the step in force, and a non-Saudi who pays nothing while the company still owes the hazards branch (4220.705791ms)
✔ the contributory wage is clamped to the floor and the ceiling the law sets, and the rate is read from the payroll month so a step-up lands on the month it takes effect (4128.141834ms)
✔ an employee with no recorded case is never guessed: the draft shows him as unavailable at zero and the run refuses to be submitted or approved, naming who is missing and who records it (4229.555542ms)
✔ a Saudi who joined after the new law but already had a contribution period elsewhere is moved back to the previous law by a dated override, and withdrawing it restores the derived case (4112.366625ms)
✔ a Gulf national is excluded by the owner decision, so he has no applicable case and blocks approval like anyone else — he is never silently treated as Saudi or as non-Saudi (3996.084333ms)
✔ the old single-rate cycle policy keeps governing the months it governed: a month before the insurance rule took effect reproduces its recorded line, and the run says which basis it used (4028.276416ms)
✔ the insurance case reveals nationality, so it is read by the same rule: a manager without the workforce capability cannot open the screen, and no override is recorded without an HR role (4138.761792ms)
✔ a joiner mid-month is charged on the days of service by the divisor the HR manager chose, and both shares follow the rounding rule he accepted in the pay rules (4129.007584ms)
✔ the run totals and the wage-protection deduction never carry the employer share: it is stored on the line as the company cost and nowhere else (4397.854959ms)
✔ the pay date a run carries is the nominal day, the day Art. 48 shifts it to, and the date actually decided — and an early payment needs two people (4095.109417ms)
✔ a holiday declared after the decision can only pull the pay date earlier, never past the date the regulation sets (4046.954667ms)
✔ an early payment can be refused by the second person, and the month is then free for a new proposal (4053.28175ms)
✔ من اعتمد صرف الرواتب لا يسجّل تنفيذه، ولو حمل تصريح المراجعة (4073.686667ms)
✔ PAY-04: a backdated raise leaves approved runs untouched and surfaces the exact difference per month, proposed once and approved by someone else (4268.611292ms)
✔ PAY-04: a rejected retro movement frees the difference to be proposed again, and an overpayment becomes a proposed deduction (4040.080209ms)
✔ regulation policies: seeded drafts cite their articles, stay inactive until the HR manager accepts them, and choices are made by the acceptor (4040.209459ms)
✔ resignation: deemed accepted by the daily job after 30 days with no reply, the clock waits for the accepted rule, and deferral is limited to 60 days with a reason (4162.646583ms)
✔ resignation: an open investigation or suspension holds acceptance until it is decided, and never blocks the letter itself (Art. 37/5) (4076.118334ms)
✔ resignation: acceptance by the authority holder opens the offboarding bundle from lifecycle, with its clearance items (4070.277584ms)
✔ settlement: both Art. 36(2) readings side by side, no approval before the HR manager chooses, unpaid leave over 20 days excluded, dues deadline and death (4055.057167ms)
✔ deduction caps: advance instalment ≤10%, court order ≤25%, fines ≤5 days a month — refused up front, and a run carrying a breach cannot move to review (4388.13725ms)
