✔ defect 4: with no adopted timer nobody is reminded and nothing lapses — and the sweep says so (4322.907417ms)
✔ defect 4: adopted timers remind the owner once per stage, tell the returner, and lapse honestly — never on the day of the first reminder (4491.739ms)
✔ review: after a decision is escalated away, the original approver is not shown «أعدتُها وتنتظر صاحبها» (4670.32375ms)
✔ review: a returned request that lapses while its owner is stopped still reaches a living person (4540.555667ms)
✔ a review route runs its stages in order: parallel stages at the same position open together, the next position opens only when all of them are decided, and three decisions exist — not two (4004.9ms)
✔ a decision belongs to one version: the author never decides, a decision is never edited, and reversing it needs a new version with its own route (4178.965958ms)
✔ changes_required stops the route at once and cancels what is left; nothing downstream is silently treated as decided (4301.07275ms)
✔ an internal annotation never reaches the client: the separation is enforced in the query, not in the screen (4752.526ms)
✔ annotations are pinned to a place in the material with relative coordinates, never pixels, and only inside the material they belong to (4507.443958ms)
✔ every annotation closes with a stated outcome, “will not fix” needs its reason, and what stays open becomes the worklist for the next version (4160.084209ms)
✔ a client stage closes only on an external approval documented against the same version; the platform opens no external review link and sends no mail (4105.686416ms)
✔ reminders and escalation stay inside the platform, are repeatable without piling up, and a route saved as a template rebuilds the same stages (4094.720833ms)
✔ tenant isolation, the capability and optimistic locking all hold, and neither screen emits inline style or script (4134.9965ms)
✔ RING: the field is a masked orthogonal lattice at 1 : 1.13, never a scatter (11.0745ms)
✔ RING: the same input always gives the same field, and an empty request is safe (13.3075ms)
✔ RING: a 300 degree arc from 12 o'clock, anticlockwise, with a 60 degree gap and the guideline ink law (6.765959ms)
✔ RING: mirror=true reverses the direction of t and the mirror flag of every node (14.363667ms)
✔ RING: the colour mix is 77 / 10 / 10 / 3 by a deterministic hash (1.972042ms)
✔ RING: exclusion rectangles delete marks and feather the ink around them (18.488708ms)
✔ RING: marks outside the canvas box are clipped, which is how the phone ring becomes a horizon (2.1835ms)
✔ RING: up to 12 moons are promoted lattice nodes at the head of the arc, in order (8.341083ms)
✔ RING: drifters live on the lattice outside the halo and never carry data (8.5235ms)
✔ COMMA: Form A is a full rectangular lattice with a horizontal fade and a mirrored left half (1.431875ms)
✔ COMMA: Form D is the logo comma cut out of Form A, about 1,500 marks at 760 x 554 (5.88225ms)
✔ BACKDROP: the control object is exact, and a failed getContext leaves eight harmless no-ops (1.515292ms)
✔ BACKDROP: off the stage the backing store is zero and nothing is scheduled (3.009292ms)
✔ BACKDROP: the phone caps DPR at 1.5 and freezes after 12 s; the desktop stops after 60 s; resume() restarts (76.807ms)
✔ BACKDROP: reduced motion draws one static frame, never calls requestAnimationFrame, and refreshes on a 60 s timer (14.154333ms)
✔ BACKDROP: pause() holds a static frame and resume() returns to the loop; a hidden document schedules nothing (3.218709ms)
✔ BACKDROP: colours come from the design tokens only, and are read again when the theme or the design changes (1.314375ms)
✔ BACKDROP: the opening plays once per session at full frame rate and lands every mark on its node (102.7365ms)
✔ BACKDROP: the governor degrades on dropped frames and ends in a static frame for the session (8.693333ms)
✔ BACKDROP: the index scene is drawn once with no animation frame, and the old exports are untouched (1.156416ms)
✔ BACKDROP: the gap closes only on proof: an explicit zero on home, the submit signal on login; null never closes it (18.271167ms)
✔ BACKDROP: new exclusions in mid-opening keep the running clock, and the opening block respects them (70.677833ms)
✔ BACKDROP: a minute tick of progress is drawn without restarting the idle ladder, even when resume() follows it (20.3825ms)
✔ BACKDROP: the hero strip leaving the viewport stops the loop, and coming back restarts it (0.595833ms)
✔ ledger dates: an expense approved by finance at 00:30 Riyadh on 1 October is dated 1 October in the journal and in the pending list, not 30 September (4317.347292ms)
✔ migration 178: a promise to pay made at 01:00 Riyadh on 1 October cannot be dated 30 September, even written past the code (4801.495458ms)
✔ riyadhToday and riyadhMonth read the Riyadh calendar at the edges: 20:59Z, 21:00Z, 23:59Z, 00:00Z, month end and year end (1.135417ms)
✔ the default clock is Date: riyadhToday() and riyadhMonth() follow a pinned clock on both sides of midnight UTC (0.414ms)
✔ riyadhDateOf passes a bare date through, and returns null for nothing or an unreadable value (0.105708ms)
✔ the ranges are half-open UTC instants: a Riyadh day, month and year start at 21:00Z of the day before (0.694625ms)
✔ ai: at 02:05 Riyadh on the 1st the month cost and the runs of the day count what happened since Riyadh midnight, not since UTC midnight (4384.396458ms)
✔ finance grants: a grant from the 1st to the 31st is live from Riyadh midnight of the 1st and ends at Riyadh midnight after the 31st (4927.988292ms)
✔ invoices: a tax invoice issued at 02:05 Riyadh on 1 January carries the new year in its number (4451.361667ms)
✔ career profile: at 02:05 Riyadh on 1 January a qualification obtained this year is accepted (4011.663917ms)
✔ catalog admin: the board day that seasons are read on is the Riyadh day (4028.154542ms)
✔ payroll payment: approved at 00:30 Riyadh on the 1st, it cannot be recorded as executed on the last day of the previous month (4347.202625ms)
✔ wage protection: a file exported at 00:30 Riyadh on the 1st cannot be recorded as uploaded on the last day of the previous month (4094.035459ms)
✔ expenses: a claim approved by finance at 02:05 Riyadh on the 1st cannot be reimbursed on the last day of the previous month (4136.116125ms)
✔ payables: a payment order approved at 02:05 Riyadh on the 1st cannot be recorded as executed on the last day of the previous month (4325.673209ms)
✔ pipeline: an opportunity created at 02:05 Riyadh on the 1st takes no activity dated the last day of the previous month (4229.400417ms)
✔ talent: results released at 02:05 Riyadh on the 1st can be appealed through the 15th, Riyadh time (4192.663667ms)
✔ request intake: a request made at 00:30 Riyadh fourteen days before today is still inside the duplicate window at 02:05 Riyadh (4302.982084ms)
✔ feedback: a one-to-one held at 02:05 Riyadh on the 1st is dated the 1st and held zero days ago (4121.1075ms)
✔ epmo report: a request opened at 00:30 Riyadh on the 1st is not open at the end of the previous month (4252.56675ms)
✔ deferred revenue: a reversal and a draw recorded at 00:30 Riyadh on the 1st are not in the sheet as of the last day of the previous month (4061.708958ms)
✔ custom fields: a field published at 02:05 Riyadh on the 1st is added after an opportunity closed on the last day of the previous month (4133.761958ms)
✔ guard patterns count the lines that broke on 1 October and not their corrected forms (1.134166ms)
✔ guard: no file reads a UTC timestamp as a Riyadh day more often than scripts/riyadh-time-baseline.json allows, and a new file starts at zero (128.255416ms)
✔ ROUTING: a request transfers to another department, and only its current owner may do it (4754.617542ms)
✔ ROUTING: assigned tasks hold the request open until they are settled by their owner (5110.536708ms)
✔ ROUTING: the service clock counts from submission and flags what is late (4310.295ms)
✔ PORTAL: an employee sees their own requests, decisions, tasks and quick services (4095.324958ms)
