✔ every module and stylesheet the interface imports is actually served (4371.015ms)
✔ defect 6: with an adopted timer a late step really moves — the power to decide goes up the ladder, the approver row is untouched, and both people are told the truth (4332.991709ms)
✔ defect 6: with no adopted timer nothing escalates, however old the step — and the result says why (4258.95025ms)
✔ defect 6: a confidential service never climbs by itself — it is recorded, the structure manager is told, and he moves it by name with a written reason (4142.544833ms)
✔ defect 6: an approver whose account is gone is a fact, not a threshold — his step moves without any timer, and never to a party of the request (4154.784ms)
✔ defect 6: the old button is named for what it does — «تذكير المعتمد» reminds the decider himself, moves nothing, and keeps its action key (4253.097916ms)
✔ structured fields: rows render as a table with an add button and a template, cells carry no name, and values are collected as typed arrays (1.847125ms)
✔ structured fields: what the campaign, scope and review-cycle forms produce is accepted by the backend as is (4046.219917ms)
✔ STR-05/06/08/09, CRT-02/08/09: approved brief, two outputs, inspected rights and internal acceptance preserve their source versions (4024.264292ms)
✔ STR-08/09: returned briefs need a new version, retain the reason, and cannot be changed after approval (4118.973417ms)
✔ CRT-04/05/08: output return and quality approval are tied to one immutable version (4041.934041ms)
✔ CRT-07/09, LEG-03, PRO-06: expired, future, short-duration and wrong-channel rights block new manifests (4167.221708ms)
✔ CRT-07/08/09: unchecked or failed assets cannot be included, and an unapproved output cannot enter an otherwise valid manifest (4057.113708ms)
✔ STR-09/CRT-04: only the project creator may appoint an independent alternate reviewer (6247.152292ms)
✔ CRT-06: tenant, admin and project membership are checked on all studio reads and actions (4270.478458ms)
✔ CRT-06/09: asset, output and package IDs cannot be substituted across studio workspaces (4061.789333ms)
✔ CRT-05/09: retries cannot duplicate a decision, manifest or acceptance; snapshots survive later output creation (4082.96075ms)
✔ STR-06/CRT-02: incomplete briefs, unknown fields, channels and external asset URLs are rejected (4314.310375ms)
✔ CRT-09: audit failure rolls back the issued manifest and the workspace version (4355.793416ms)
✔ CRT-06: createOnce rechecks membership for a repeated studio creation (4037.255ms)
✔ CRT-07/09: acceptance rechecks asset expiry across midnight in Riyadh (4340.294583ms)
✔ STR-09/CRT-04: membership and current role revoke a designated reviewer before the next decision (4285.381834ms)
✔ CRT-05 UI: output forms capture the original target and version without editable identity fields (4130.0305ms)
✔ CRT-06/09 UI: unauthorized actions are absent, content is escaped, and an asset reference is never a download link (4149.95425ms)
✔ commencement: only an independent reviewer in scope issues, replaces or withdraws it — never the requester, an outsider, another tenant or a conflicted reviewer (4381.866041ms)
✔ commencement: it records issuer, dates, scope, order version, validity and evidence, and the receipt re-checks all of it when it is recorded (4265.223083ms)
✔ commencement: withdrawal and replacement add records and never rewrite or delete the earlier ones (4140.988792ms)
✔ commencement: a replayed or repeated request creates no second record, through the module and through the API route (5086.804958ms)
✔ commencement: a receipt racing a withdrawal never lands after it — separate processes on one database file (8176.372416ms)
ℹ orderings: fresh:withdraw fresh:withdraw fresh:withdraw same:receive same:receive same:receive
✔ commencement UI: the purchase shows the standing authorisation and its history, and every form posts to the procurement route with the opened version (4390.800834ms)
✔ migration 162: an authorisation issued before it is carried as issued — no validity or evidence invented — and opens no receipt until replaced (3224.701916ms)
✔ synthetic month: September 2026 runs end to end through the real paths — sales, procurement, advances, expenses, bank import with grouped and split matches and a posted fee, a zero-difference reconciliation, a green close, a controlled reopen, a dated adjustment and a re-close — and proves itself (4685.858959ms)
✔ TAL-05: weights must total 100, the cycle opens one review per employee with an active manager, and scores stay hidden from the employee until release (4177.854416ms)
✔ TAL-06: calibration is by a third person, a changed score needs a reason, release is not by the cycle creator, and one appeal is decided by someone who neither scored nor calibrated (4156.498417ms)
✔ TAL-07/08: training is approved by the manager and completed with evidence; a goal is closed by the manager, not by its owner (4136.377958ms)
✔ TAL-09: succession plans are visible only to their capability holders, never to the position holder or a listed candidate (4025.480875ms)
✔ tax rates: the platform ships with none, a rate carries its source and confirmation date, the person who enters it does not confirm it, and a period keeps its own rate (4107.05ms)
✔ vat worksheet: the preparer never reviews it, an unexplained gap against the ledger blocks closing, and a reviewed worksheet is corrected by a new revision (4147.478875ms)
✔ vat worksheet: figures come from the ledger, unverified input vat never enters the worksheet, and the CSV boxes are named by the user (4046.849584ms)
✔ withholding: the rate comes from a dated confirmed setting at the payment date, the classifier is recorded by name, and whoever records it does not document its remittance (4303.037958ms)
✔ zakat worksheet: the platform names no line and computes no pool, and the specialist’s worksheet is approved by someone other than its preparer (6220.714792ms)
✔ both screens render for the preparer and the reviewer, every offered button opens a usable form, and each screen states it is a worksheet and not a return (4150.836ms)
✔ technical proposal gate requires an immutable approved checklist before quote review (3995.726375ms)
✔ EPMO reviews every item, records owned gaps, and permits a corrected revision (4203.985667ms)
✔ commercial screen exposes the source checklist and the independent EPMO review form (4212.444291ms)
